From: OpenWrt prplmesh package
Subject: [PATCH] agent: fill a missing client BSSID from the reporting VAP

On stock OpenWrt the nl80211 HAL reports STA_Connected with an all-zero
BSSID in two cases: stations imported by the STA-FIRST/STA-NEXT sweep of
already connected clients, and live associations when hostapd did not
hand over the (re)association frame (notify_mgmt_frames=0, the stock
default). The agent then finds no radio for the zero BSSID and drops the
association, so the controller never learns about the client and client
steering cannot work.

The VAP the station was reported on is always known: use its MAC as the
BSSID when the HAL did not provide one.

---
--- a/agent/src/beerocks/fronthaul_manager/ap_manager/ap_manager.cpp
+++ b/agent/src/beerocks/fronthaul_manager/ap_manager/ap_manager.cpp
@@ -2807,6 +2807,18 @@
         notification->bssid()        = msg->params.bssid;
         notification->capabilities() = msg->params.capabilities;
 
+        // On stock OpenWrt hostapd may not hand the (re)association frame to
+        // the HAL, and the STA-FIRST/STA-NEXT sweep of already connected
+        // stations carries no BSSID at all. A zero BSSID makes the agent drop
+        // the association (no radio matches it), so the client never reaches
+        // the controller. The VAP the station was reported on is known: use
+        // its MAC as the BSSID.
+        if (notification->bssid() == beerocks::net::network_utils::ZERO_MAC) {
+            notification->bssid() = tlvf::mac_from_string(vap_node->second.mac);
+            LOG(DEBUG) << "STA_Connected without BSSID, using VAP " << vap_node->second.bss
+                       << " BSSID " << notification->bssid();
+        }
+
         notification->multi_ap_profile()   = msg->params.multi_ap_profile;
         notification->is_mlo()             = msg->params.is_mlo;
         notification->mlo_modes()          = msg->params.mlo_modes;
